Ticket #4471 combines reports about dates shown on the wrong day. The export has overlapping
rows, so counts below deduplicate by report ID before grouping.

## Problems

The reports split into two causes. The intake tag is only a guess; the tenant locale, booking
form, and channel determine the cause.

### Shared parser reads dates month first

For tenants whose locale writes the day before the month, the shared parser flips day and month.
This cause appears across app, email, and booking-v2 form reports. The reports in this group
are tracked in [the shared parser ticket](https://github.com/sebadab1/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

### booking-v3 hint conflicts with day-first locales

The booking-v3 form tells people to enter month first, while its tenant locale reads dates day
first. This separate form-hint problem affects booking-v3 form reports only. The reports are
tracked in [the booking-v3 hint ticket](https://github.com/sebadab1/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1);
do not merge it with the shared parser issue.

## Count and evidence

This table preserves the original export's desk ownership. Its “no ticket of its own”
label describes that snapshot, before the separate follow-up tickets linked above.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table counts unique reports by the tenant and form rules in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`. The five
one-day-move reports in `desk-notes.json` remain included in their parser group; they are not a
third cause. Intake tags can disagree with the cause, so they do not determine the issue split.

